 	<TEXT>
 		<Tag>TXT_KEY_SPY_UNIT_GENERIC_DESCRIPTION_WITH_INFO_ON_ALL_CIVS_NO_CIV_PEDIA</Tag>
 		<English>[TAB]Spies differ greatly from most units. Completely invisible to enemy Civilizations, Spies can enter enemy territory to perform one Espionage Mission per turn. Active missions are tile sensitive, meaning you will have to sneak your Spy onto the enemy improvement or city you wish to affect. Performing a mission costs a certain number of Espionage Points and will cause an indicator to pop-up for your opponent over the location of the mission, informing him of the act (but not necessarily of your Spy). If the mission succeeds, the Spy may  survive to perform more Missions, or she may be caught and destroyed. If the mission fails, the Spy will be destroyed, but no Espionage Points will be consumed. The cost of these Espionage Missions decrease the longer a Spy remains stationary on a tile, but every turn a Spy remains in enemy territory, there is a chance that she will be caught and destroyed. The chances of being caught increase with your opponent's Espionage spending, with the presence of a Security Bureau and if your Spy has recently performed a mission against that tile. If the Spy is caught, there is also a chance that its owner will be revealed.[PARAGRAPH:1]In addition to performing Espionage Missions, Spies also make excellent intelligence gatherers. They can use enemy roads and enter the cities of opponents with whom the player is at war, allowing the player access to otherwise unreachable information. The downside is that spies have a chance to get caught when they end their turn in unwelcome territory, even if they perform no active missions. Unwelcome territory is any territory belonging to a rival with whom you do not have an open borders agreement.[PARAGRAPH:2][BOLD]Missions[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:1]To perform an Espionage Mission, a player must move a Spy unit to the plot or city where they would like to perform the mission and select the Espionage Mission button.[PARAGRAPH:1]The Espionage Missions are:[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Sabotage Improvement[\BOLD] - Destroy an enemy improvement or route[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Sabotage Building[\BOLD] - Destroy a building within an enemy city[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Steal Treasury[\BOLD] - Steal a portion of your opponent's treasury, between 10 and 100%%[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Spread Culture[\BOLD] - Increase your cultural influence in a city[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Poison Water[\BOLD] - Temporarily increase the amount of unhealthiness within an enemy city[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Foment Unhappiness[\BOLD] - Temporarily increase unhappiness within an enemy city[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Support City Revolt[\BOLD] - Send a city into revolt for one turn. This lowers enemy city defense, but does not remove cultural borders[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Steal Technology[\BOLD] - Steal a technology from an opponent[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Sabotage Production[\BOLD] - Destroys all hammers accumulated towards construction in a city[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Sabotage Project[\BOLD] - Destroys an already completed Spaceship Part[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Influence Civics[\BOLD] - Switch one opponent's civic to match a civic you have adopted[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Influence Religion[\BOLD] - Switch an opponent's state religion to your state religion[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Perform Counterespionage[\BOLD] - Temporarily doubles cost of enemy espionage missions[PARAGRAPH:2][BOLD]Passive Missions[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:1]Passive Missions activate automatically as you accumulate certain levels of Espionage Points against an opponent. But as your opponent increases his own cache of Espionage Points, the Point costs of your Passive Missions increase in kind, requiring you to up your own Espionage spending to keep the effects. [PARAGRAPH:1]The Passive Missions are:[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Can See Demographics[\BOLD] - Allows you to see enemy demographics on the Info Screen[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Can See Research[\BOLD] - Allows you to see what your opponent is researching and how many turns they have until completion[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]City Visibility[\BOLD] - Enemy cities are added to your visibility[NEWLINE][TAB][BOLD]Investigate City[\BOLD] - You may enter enemy city screens by double-clicking on them.</English>
