+		<Tag>TXT_KEY_BUILDING_PORTUGAL_PEIXARIA_PEDIA</Tag>
+		<English>[TAB]Peixaria is the Portuguese word for an establishment that sells fish, broadly equivalent to a fish shop or fishmonger's. Such businesses form part of the distribution side of a fishing economy: fish and shellfish are landed, preserved or transported, and then sold through markets and shops to consumers who may live far from the coast.[PARAGRAPH:1]Fishing has long been important to communities along the Portuguese coast. At Armacao de Pera in the Algarve, for example, fishermen were historically attracted by abundant tuna and sardines; after being salted, the catch was sold for consumption in southern and central Portugal. Preservation, transport, and retail markets therefore linked coastal fishing communities with consumers across a much wider area.</English>
